      "canonical_url": "https://mathdb.com/p/379622/positive-coefficient-conjecture-for-adjacent-edges-in-indepe",
      "title": "Positive-coefficient conjecture for adjacent edges in independence polynomials",
      "statement": "Let $\\mathsf K_n$ be the complete graph and let $Z(\\mathbf I\\mathsf K_n;\\mathbf y)$ be the partition function of its independent-set system. For edges $e,f$, let $\\Delta Z\\{e,f\\}$ denote the Rayleigh difference. **Adjacent-edge coefficient conjecture.** If $e$ and $f$ are adjacent edges in $\\mathsf K_n$, then $\\Delta Z(\\mathbf I\\mathsf K_n)\\{e,f\\}$ has nonnegative coefficients. The claim has been checked for $n\\leq6$ and is open in general.",
      "statement_completeness": "full",
