      "title": "Efficient oracle recognition of binary internally 4-connected matroids",
      "statement": "An **internally $4$-connected matroid** is a matroid satisfying the internal $4$-connectivity condition used in the source. An oracle algorithm accesses a matroid through an oracle for its relevant operations or queries.\n\n**Binary-recognition conjecture.** There is an efficient oracle algorithm for deciding whether an internally $4$-connected matroid is binary.\n\nThe conjecture is motivated by the absence of an efficient oracle algorithm for recognizing binary matroids in general, attributed in the source to degeneracies caused by low connectivity. The source calls it ambitious and gives no resolution.",
